{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And He remembered the days of old.</b> That passed." "<b>[Moses, His people].</b> The days of Moses and His people, like שמש ירח עמד (Habakkuk 3:11). And it is possible that משה is a verb, for he draws Israel out. But the first is correct." "<b>Where is He who set them aloft.</b> The meaning: now the nations say, where is He who brought them up from the Sea of Reeds." "<b>The shepherd of His flock.</b> The people of Moses, who is the shepherd of Israel." "<b>Where is HaShem.</b> In the midst of Moses. And some say: the Glory that was in the midst of Israel."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:48.749011558Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}